{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gen-6-1","title":"Genesis 6:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The wickedness of the world, which provoked God's wrath, and caused the flood. 8 Noah finds grace. 9 His generations, etc. 14 The order, form, dimensions, and end of the ark.</p>\n<p>A.M. 1556. B.C. 2448. to multiply. 1:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-2","title":"Genesis 6:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the sons. 4:26; Ex 4:22,23; De 14:1; Ps 82:6,7; Isa 63:16; Mal 2:11; Joh 8:41 Joh 8:42; Ro 9:7,8; 2Co 6:18 saw. 2Pe 2:14 that they. 3:6; 39:6,7; 2Sa 11:2; Job 31:1; 1Jo 2:16 and they. 24:3; 27:46; Ex 34:16; De 7:3,4; Jos 23:12,13; Ezr 9:1,2,12 Ne 13:24-27; Mal 2:15; 1Co 7:39; 2Co 6:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-3","title":"Genesis 6:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>My. Nu 11:17; Ne 9:30; Isa 5:4; 63:10; Jer 11:7,11; Ac 7:51; Ga 5:16,17 1Th 5:19; 1Pe 3:18-20; Jude 1:14,15 is. Ps 78:39; Joh 3:6; Ro 8:1-13; Ga 5:16-24; 1Pe 3:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-4","title":"Genesis 6:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>giants. Nu 13:33; De 2:20,21; 3:11; 1Sa 17:4; 2Sa 21:15-22 after. 3 men of. 11:4; Nu 16:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-5","title":"Genesis 6:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>God. 13:13; 18:20,21; Ps 14:1-4; 53:2; Ro 1:28-31; 3:9-19 every imagination. or, the whole imagination.The Hebrew word signifies not only the imagination, but also the purposes and desires.</p>\n<p>8:21; De 29:19; Job 15:16; Pr 6:18; Ec 7:29; 9:3; Jer 17:9 Eze 8:9,12; Mt 15:19; Mr 7:21-23; Eph 2:1-3; Tit 3:3 thoughts. Jer 4:14 continually. Heb. every day.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-6","title":"Genesis 6:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>repented. Ex 32:14; Nu 23:19; De 32:36; 1Sa 15:11,29; 2Sa 24:16; 1Ch 21:15 Ps 106:45; 110:4; Jer 18:8-10; 26:19; Ho 11:8; Jon 3:10; Mal 3:6 Ro 11:29; Heb 6:17,18; Jas 1:17 grieved. De 5:29; 32:29; Ps 78:40; 81:13; 95:10; 119:158; Isa 48:18; 63:10 Eze 33:11; Lu 19:41,42; Eph 4:30; Heb 3:10,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-7","title":"Genesis 6:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I will. Ps 24:1,2; 37:20; Pr 10:27; 16:4 both man, and beast. Heb. from man unto beast. Jer 4:22-27; 12:3,4; Ho 4:3; Zep 1:3; Ro 3:20-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-8","title":"Genesis 6:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>19:19; Ex 33:12-17; Ps 84:11; 145:20; Pr 3:4; 8:35; 12:2; Jer 31:2 Lu 1:30; Ac 7:46; Ro 4:4; 11:6; 1Co 15:10; Ga 1:15; 2Ti 1:18 Tit 2:11; 3:7; Heb 4:16; 2Pe 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-9","title":"Genesis 6:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>These. 2:4; 5:1; 10:1 just. 7:1; Job 12:4; Pr 4:18; Ec 7:20; Eze 14:14,20; Hab 2:4; Lu 2:25 Lu 23:50; Ac 10:22; Ro 1:17; Ga 3:11; Heb 11:7; 2Pe 2:5 perfect. or, upright. 2Ch 15:17; 25:2; Job 1:1,8; Ps 37:37; Lu 1:6; Php 3:9-15 and Noah. 5:22,24; 17:1; 48:15; 1Ki 3:6; Lu 1:6; 1Pe 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-10","title":"Genesis 6:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>A.M. 1556. B.C. 2448. Shem. 5:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-11","title":"Genesis 6:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>before. 7:1; 10:9; 13:13; 2Ch 34:27; Lu 1:6; Ro 2:13; 3:19 filled. Ps 11:5; 55:9; 140:11; Isa 60:18; Jer 6:7; Eze 8:17; 28:16; Ho 4:1,2 Hab 1:2; 2:8,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-12","title":"Genesis 6:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>God. 8; 18:21; Job 33:27; Ps 14:2; 33:13,14; 53:2,3; Pr 15:3 for all. 4,5; 7:1,21; 9:12,16,17; Job 22:15-17; Lu 3:6; 1Pe 3:19,20; 2Pe 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-13","title":"Genesis 6:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>The end. Jer 51:13; Eze 7:2-6; Am 8:2; 1Pe 4:7 filled. 4,11,12; 49:5; Ho 4:1,2 and behold. 17 with. or, from. 7:23 the earth. Jer 4:23-28; Heb 11:7; 2Pe 3:6,7,10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-14","title":"Genesis 6:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>A.M. 1536. B.C. 2468. Make. Mt 24:38; Lu 17:27; 1Pe 3:20 rooms. Heb. nests. shalt pitch. Ex 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-15","title":"Genesis 6:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>cubits. 7:20; De 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-16","title":"Genesis 6:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>window. 8:6; 2Sa 6:16; 2Ki 9:30 the door. 7:16; Lu 13:25 with. Eze 41:16; 42:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-17","title":"Genesis 6:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>behold. 13; 7:4,21-23; 9:9; Ex 14:17; Le 26:28; De 32:39; Ps 29:10; Isa 51:12 Eze 5:8; 6:3; 34:11,20; Ho 5:14; 2Pe 2:5 bring. 7:4,17,21-23; Job 22:16; Ps 29:10; 93:3,4; 107:34; Isa 54:9; Am 9:6 Mt 24:39; Lu 17:27; Heb 11:7; 1Pe 3:20 is the. 2:7; 7:15 shall die. 7; Ps 107:34; Ro 5:12-14,21; 6:23; 8:20-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-18","title":"Genesis 6:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>establish. 9:9,11; 17:4,7,21 come. 7:1,7,13; Isa 26:20; Heb 11:7; 1Pe 3:20; 2Pe 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-19","title":"Genesis 6:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>The cubit being nearly 22 inches, and the ark being 300 cubits in length, 50 in breadth, and 30 in height, (ver. 15,) its size was equal to 547 feet long, 91 feet broad, and 54 feet high; and it is computed to had been 81,062 tons burthen. These dimensions were sufficient to contain all the persons and animals in it, and food for more than a year.</p>\n<p>two. 7:2,3,8,9,15,16; 8:17; Ps 36:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-20","title":"Genesis 6:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>fowls. 1:20-24; Ac 10:11,12 two. 1:28; 2:19; 7:8-16; Joh 5:40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-21","title":"Genesis 6:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>1:29,30; Job 38:41; 40:20; Ps 35:6; 104:27,28; 136:25; 145:16; 147:9 Mt 6:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-6-22","title":"Genesis 6:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>7:5,9,16; 17:23; Ex 40:16,19,21,23,25,27,32; De 12:32; Mt 7:24-27 Joh 2:5; 15:14; Heb 11:7,8; 1Jo 5:3,4</p>"}]}